# Async Jobs & Provider Sagas

Long-running or dual-write provider work goes through `async_jobs`, not request transactions.

## Required sequence

```text
intent row + async_jobs enqueue → COMMIT
→ worker claim (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) → COMMIT claim
→ provider I/O
→ reconcile DB → success | retry | DLQ
```

## Must

- Stable per-tenant `idempotency_key`
- Leases + expired-lease reclaim; never leave work permanently stuck
- Handlers idempotent / safely re-entrant
- `TenantContext` from the job row
- Graceful SIGTERM: stop claiming; finish or release current work

## Must not

- Call Twilio / LiveKit / Stripe inside an open business TX
- Claim success without reconciliation
- Process the same job concurrently on two workers
- Use production credentials for destructive sandbox tests

Run workers: `python -m callbot_platform.workers.run_jobs`

See: `docs/SAGA_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/WORKER_OPERATIONS.md`
